===A4_S3_D2===
// attach to door of farmhouse
Narrator: Inside the farmhouse, Clara prepares a quick pot of tea, mentioning that it’s from the Viridi.
Clara: Their knowledge of the forest really is such a blessing! I think you’ve probably met her — Chione has taken up the mantle of studying plants after her master retired, and was the one to mix these packets of dried flowers and herbs. #portrait:Clara
Narrator: Amelia leans forward from her chair, reading the label.
Amelia: ‘Good for relaxation and calming the mind before sleep.’ #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Clara: Normally I like the ones for sharpening the senses more, but since we have a fourth guest on the way… #portrait:Clara
Narrator: Two knocks echo on the door.
Cillian: Good evening, all. #portrait:Cillian
Clara: That’s him! #portrait:Clara
Narrator: Cillian introduces himself to you and Amelia, explaining that he was busy sorting out some business to do with the floods.
Cillian: As Elder Silas might’ve informed, there are a couple of artifacts in our possession that might be of interest to you. And a certain box that we’ve never been able to open. #portrait:Cillian
+[Not even by force?]
    -> choiceforce
+[What is the mechanism like?]
    -> choicemechanism

===choiceforce===
Cillian: Well… we didn’t want to damage it too much. And as it was made of metal, one can’t be sure if the item inside would survive such force, or even melting by fire. #portrait:Cillian
->afterchoiceA4S3

===choiceletsdoit===
Cillian: The box is made of metal, and seems to contain a type of puzzle element with its key. #portrait:Cillian
->afterchoiceA4S3

===afterchoiceA4S3===
Cillian: To this day, we’ve haven’t found information that reveals its purpose or technique, either, so we’re at a bit of a loss. #portrait:Cillian
Narrator: Since it’s never been opened before though, Cillian reassures you that there’s no pressure if you can’t figure it out. You can start tomorrow when you’re rested.
Cillian: Since you were from an island of only humans… Is there anything you’d like to ask me in particular? #portrait:Cillian
Narrator: Truthfully, you could think of a million questions if you tried. But one thing stands out…
Noelle: How did the Krakenfolk come about? #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: I’ve only heard that they appeared after Noah’s time… and while I may be one of them, my home island has never encountered such a transformation before. #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: (And of course, <i>I</i> have to be the first that gets thrown out.) #portrait:NoelleUm
Cillian: I see… #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: I suppose right after Noah’s encounter with the kraken would be the best place to start. #portrait:Cillian
Narrator: <i>During the battle between kraken and crew, the Great Disaster’s blood was shed and flowed into the ocean.</i>
Narrator: Over time, this would spread far and wide — ultimately, it is impossible for living beings to not have consumed it in some form.
Narrator: That is not the singular cause, however. Only humans — non-adapted ones — would be susceptible to transforming into a Krakenfolk. Which could be triggered if they ingested a certain metallic compound.
Cillian: The compound is rare, however, and can only be found in the deep ocean. #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: Considering your descriptions, it seems like the chalice you drank from may have been contaminated by it in some way. #portrait:Cillian
Noelle: (In the deep ocean…) #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: No way. Could it have been when your father went scavenging?
Narrator: Your heart twists, and it starts becoming hard to breathe.
Cillian: …There is no reversal for becoming a Krakenfolk. #portrait:Cillian
Noelle: I see… #portrait:NoelleUm
Cillian: But they do gain a variety of new abilities, far beyond the evolution of regular Thavma. #portrait:Cillian
Clara: Right! They have enhanced strength, can breathe underwater… #portrait:Clara
Clara: I’ve heard that their hair can even glow, and that the most skilled can control their tentacles as separate limbs! #portrait:Clara
Narrator: Amelia hums.
Amelia: Much cooler than being a plain old human. #portrait:AmeliaHappy
Narrator: You laugh, appreciating their efforts to comfort you.
Noelle: If those are all true, then I really should be putting those skills to use. Or learning them, at least. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Cillian: The Ichthyos can help with that. #portrait:Cillian
Narrator: Cillian explains that whenever a new Krakenfolk came around, the Ichthyos would be the first to volunteer ‘training’ them.
Clara: They can be a little energetic, but they mean well and protect the waters around Thavmia. #portrait:Clara
Clara: It’s safe to say that their work and the Viridi’s go hand in hand. #portrait:Clara
Amelia: I haven’t actually met the Ichthyos before. Only seen some in passing when they visited inland. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Clara: Oh, that’s rare! Staying out of water for too long dries their skin, so they’re more inclined to the ocean, since rivers are, uh… #portrait:Clara
Cillian: Not built for diving. #portrait:Cillian
Narrator: Their expressions tell you that despite this, some Icthyos might have tried.
Noelle: I look forward to meeting them eventually. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Cillian: Feel free to make yourself at home. #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: We’ve put up one of our tents in the village for you. It should be the same appearance as the one from the Viridi. #portrait:Cillian
Amelia: How’d you know? #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Cillian: Well, that’s because… Our very own weaver, Rowan, handed them out to us as camping gear. #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: They’re prototypes for the tents he’s going to make in bulk for the caverns. #portrait:Cillian
Cillian: The yellow helps remind us of the sun, no? #portrait:Cillian
Cillain: Details like that are important when you’re shut into the mountains for days. #portrait:Cillian
Clara: We hope the guestroom will be to your liking! #portrait:Clara
Narrator: As if on cue, your stomach rumbles. Clara chuckles.
Clara: We can find something for that too. #portrait:Clara
// next, go to sleep. No dream
->DONE